meta:
  origin:
    # Data product / Snapshot
    title: Top wealth shares in the UK over more than a century
    description: |-
      This dataset presents long-run estimates of the concentration of personal wealth in the United Kingdom, measured as the share of total net personal wealth held by top wealth groups from 1895 onwards.

      The estimates are constructed mainly from estate data (wealth left at death) using the estate multiplier method, by which estates are re-weighted to represent the living population, and are linked with earlier investment-income and other administrative sources to extend the series back over more than a century.

      The series cover cumulative top shares — the shares of the top 10%, top 5%, top 1%, top 0.5% and top 0.1% of adults, together with the complementary share of the bottom 90% — as well as the intermediate brackets that lie between these thresholds.
    date_published: "2018-06-01"

    # Citation
    producer: Alvaredo, Atkinson and Morelli
    citation_full: |-
      Alvaredo, F., Atkinson, A. B., & Morelli, S. (2018). Top wealth shares in the UK over more than a century. Journal of Public Economics, 162, 26-47. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpubeco.2018.02.008

    # Files
    url_main: https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpubeco.2018.02.008
    date_accessed: '2026-07-28'

